Source: xsawyerx/guacamole (Guacamole v0.008) at 2838253, its t/ suite.

Produced by running, from the pvm repository root, with perl 5.42.0:

    perl internal/chart/testdata/guacamole/extract.pl <checkout of xsawyerx/guacamole at 2838253>

extract.pl runs every t/**/*.t with this directory ahead of Guacamole's own
lib on @INC, so the recording Guacamole/Test.pm here writes each parses and
parsent argument instead of parsing it. Test/Fatal.pm is a load-only
stand-in: three tests import Test::Fatal and none call it.

- parses/, parsent/: one case file per unique argument text, first
  occurrence wins, named <test path>-<NNN>.pl. Each file is preamble.pl (one
  line) followed by the argument byte for byte, so trailing whitespace and a
  missing final newline are Guacamole's, and the whitespace pre-commit hooks
  exclude these directories.
- stubs/: one module for each module a parses case uses that perl cannot
  find, each with $VERSION '9999', above every version a case requests.

Which cases perl accepts is not recorded here: the pinned perl's labels are
internal/chart/testdata/labels/in-tree.txt, written by
internal/chart/offline/label.sh.

Nothing in pvm reads the Guacamole checkout after extraction; rerunning the
command above regenerates this directory exactly.
